.TH SCHSYM 5
.SH NAME
schsym \- symbols, pin tables and sheets of schematics
.SH DESCRIPTION
The library holds three kinds of file.
They are looked up in the project first (symbols and sheets next to
the source), then in the libraries of the program.
.SS Shapes
.IB symbols / KIND .sym
draws one kind of symbol, a record a line, in points (72 to the inch)
from the origin of the shape; # starts a comment, and a line that ends
in a backslash goes on on the next:
.PP
.RS
.nf
prefix R
pin NAME X Y WAY
box X0 Y0 X1 Y1
side right|above|left|below
swap NAME...
flip NAME NAME
flag ground|chassis|supply|port|global
width W                 the weight of the lines after it (0.5)
line X Y X Y ...        a line
loop X Y X Y ...        a closed line
fill X Y X Y ...        a filled polygon
blank X Y X Y ...       a polygon filled with the paper
circle X Y R            a circle
disk X Y R              a filled circle
.fi
.RE
.PP
A pin is the end of a lead, at X Y in units of the grid, 0.1 in (7.2
points), and a wire leaves it the way WAY points (r, u, l or d).
The box, in units of the grid, is the body that wires and other parts
keep out of, the pins left out.
The prefix starts the designators; the side is where the text of the
part goes as the shape stands; the swap list names pins that may
trade places; the flip pair trades places when the part is flipped.
A drawing record after the word
.B flip
is drawn only when the part is flipped, and after
.B plain
only when it is not: the signs of an op amp's inputs.
A flag names a net instead of being a part.
.PP
.nf
# resistor.sym -- a resistor, IEEE 315 zigzag
prefix R
pin 1 0 2 u
pin 2 0 -2 d
box -0.45 -1.5 0.45 1.5
side right
swap 1 2
line 0 14.4 0 7.08 -2.07 5.9 2.07 3.54 -2.07 1.18 2.07 -1.18 ...
.fi
.SS Pin tables
.IB symbols / maker / part
gives the pins of one part number, in lower case:
.PP
.RS
.nf
shape opamp
prefix U
pin NAME NUMBER
nc NUMBER...
.fi
.RE
.PP
Each pin of the shape takes a number of the package; nc lists the
pins of the package on no pin of the shape.
A part whose value is a part number with a pin table is drawn by its
shape and numbered by its table.
The pins of a shape without a table are numbered by their names.
.SS Sheets
.IB sheets / NAME .sheet
draws the border and the title block of one paper, in points from its
lower left corner, and says where the drawing goes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
paper W H
room X0 Y0 X1 Y1
clear body|text|label|flag D
line X Y X Y ...
text F S A J X Y TEXT
.fi
.RE
.PP
A text is a text record of
.IR vec (5);
a $ in it and the rest of the line name a field (Title, Rev, Date,
Drawn from the source; Page and File made), which the sheet shows in
its place, or nothing if it is empty.
The clear records are the room the drawing keeps, D points at scale 1,
which the placer, the router and the label placer of
.IR schdraw (1)
keep and any checker measures: body, between a wire and the body of a
part not on its net, and between two bodies; text, between a label and
any wire, body or other label; label, from a body to its own label; and
flag, round a flag, which labels keep off.
A sheet must give all four.
.SH SEE ALSO
schdraw(1), sch(5)
